menu "Airspy development"
config AIRSPY_FFT_SERVER
    bool "Advertise SpyServer FFT stream"
    depends on !AIRSPY_SPECTRUM_CAPTURE_TEST
    default n
    help
        Enables FFT+IQ with independently tuned I/Q. Narrow FFT settings can
        heavily load the USB core; monitor dropped blocks under actual load.
config AIRSPY_FFT_BENCHMARK
    bool "Run temporary on-device FFT benchmark"
    default n
    help
        Runs a timed synthetic FFT workload for performance validation.
        Keep disabled in normal receiver firmware.
config AIRSPY_FFT_CAPTURE_TEST
    bool "Run temporary live USB spectrum capture test"
    default n
    help
        Captures occasional real I/Q blocks and computes spectra without
        advertising an FFT stream. Keep disabled in normal firmware.
config AIRSPY_SPECTRUM_CAPTURE_TEST
    bool "Run continuous zoomed spectrum pipeline test"
    default n
    help
        Processes complete USB blocks in a bounded nonblocking worker.
        This diagnostic does not advertise a SpyServer FFT stream.
config AIRSPY_SPECTRUM_TEST_STAGE
    int "Spectrum test decimation stage"
    depends on AIRSPY_SPECTRUM_CAPTURE_TEST
    range 0 6
    default 3
config AIRSPY_IQ_BALANCE
    bool "Apply static IQ-imbalance (image-rejection) correction"
    default n
    help
        Estimates the Airspy HF+ I/Q gain and phase imbalance from the streaming
        signal and applies a Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization at the full sample
        rate, improving image rejection and thus SNR when a strong signal sits
        in the image band. Not yet hardware-validated; disable it if the client
        (e.g. SDROxide) already applies its own IQ correction.

config AIRSPY_IQ_BALANCE_FREQ
    bool "Apply frequency-domain adaptive IQ-imbalance correction"
    depends on !AIRSPY_IQ_BALANCE
    default n
    help
        Frequency-domain port of the upstream libairspyhf iqbalancer.c: cancels
        DC, correlates each FFT bin with its image, and adapts the phase and
        amplitude correction with a perturbed line search. Robust to DC offset
        and to asymmetric spectra that bias the static whole-signal estimate.
        Runs a few FFT passes per second on the USB core. Disable it if the
        client already applies its own IQ correction.
config AIRSPY_DC_REMOVE
    bool "Remove the baseband DC offset (DC blocker)"
    default n
    help
        Applies a first-order high-pass (~12 Hz cutoff at 768 kS/s) to the raw
        I/Q stream, removing the HF+ LO-leakage DC spike at the passband center.
        This un-masks weak signals within a few Hz of center and keeps the DC
        offset from biasing the IQ-imbalance estimate. It also attenuates any
        signal within ~12 Hz of the center frequency.
endmenu
